<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43809" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sēquăna</span></b> , ae,
			f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>one of the principal rivers of</i> Gallia Celtica, <i>the Seine</i>, <i><span class="en">Caes. B. G. 1,
				1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7, 57</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7, 58</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mel. 3, 2,
			4</span></i>; <i>masc.</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 17,
				31, § 105</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sēquă-ni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the dwellers on the</i> Sequana, <i><span class="en">Caes. B. G. 1,
				1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 9</span></i>; 1, 10; 1, 31; 1,
			35; 1, 44; 4, 10; 6, 12; 7, 66; <i><span class="en">Cic. Att.
				1, 19, 2</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sēquănus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to the</i> Sequani: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gens,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					1, 425</span></i>
			:  ager, <i><span class="en">Plin. 14, 1,
				3, § 18</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sēquănī-cus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of the</i> Sequani:
			textrix. <i><span class="en">Mart. 4, 19, 1</span></i>.</div>
